.page getopts 1 parse options in shell scripts

# SYNOPSIS
*getopts* _OPTSTRING_ _NAME_ [_ARGUMENT_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`getopts` is a gapsh builtin for scripts that take options. Each call looks at the next option among the _ARGUMENT_s (the positional parameters if none are given), stores its letter in the variable _NAME_ and updates `OPTIND`. _OPTSTRING_ lists the option letters; a letter followed by a colon takes an argument, which is stored in `OPTARG`. An unknown letter is stored as `?`. The status is 0 while there are options and 1 when they have run out (at the first word that does not start with a dash, or at `--`).

# EXAMPLES
    while getopts "ab:" o; do
        case $o in
            a) echo "-a given";;
            b) echo "-b says $OPTARG";;
            \?) echo "bad option";;
        esac
    done

# SEE ALSO
shift(1), set(1), gapsh-language(7)
